# Force LF line endings for the shell scripts and the Dockerfile so the
# container entrypoint works on Linux regardless of the cloner's
# core.autocrlf setting. On Windows, `core.autocrlf=true` (the default)
# converts the repo's LF to CRLF at checkout; a CRLF shebang
# (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`) makes the kernel look for a `bash\r`
# interpreter that does not exist, so the container exits immediately.
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf for these files and keeps them LF on every
# platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
